  "verbalization": "Sargachromanol M is consistently shown to have a target relationship with CEM/C2, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including (16alpha,20R,22S,23S)-16,23:22,25-diepoxy-2,20,22,23-tetrahydroxycucurbita-1,5-diene-3,11-dione 2-O-beta-D-glucopyranoside, 1-Hydroxy-2,6-dimethoxyanthracene-9,10-dione, and Prim-O-Glucosylcimifugin. All these compounds share a common target, CX-1, suggesting a potential pathway where Sargachromanol M may influence the activity of CEM/C2 through these intermediates. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where Sargachromanol M acts as a modulator of CEM/C2, which in turn interacts with CX-1. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the consistent association with CX-1 indicate that Sargachromanol M may exert its biological effects through a mechanism involving CEM/C2, potentially by modulating the activity of CX-1 or other downstream targets. This integrated evidence suggests that Sargachromanol M may be a key player in the regulation of CX-1 through a complex network of interactions involving CEM/C2 and its associated compounds.",
